*** 26.2.0 features

- The :tool:`htcondor annex` commands *create* and *add* are now treated
  equivalently and can be issued before any jobs for the named annex have
  been submitted.
  :jira:`3931`

- When running Docker universe jobs, the execute event is now logged
  when the container is *started*, not when it is *created*.  The
  container start may take some time, so this makes various statistics
  more accurate, and allows :tool:`condor_ssh_to_job` to have a better
  idea when the container is actually running.
  :jira:`3966`

- Docker universe jobs now have :ad-attr:`DockerImageHash` recorded
  in the job ad for provenance reasons.
  :jira:`974`
  
*** 26.2.0 bugs

- Removed the old DAG file parser and the ``DAGMAN_USE_OLD_FILE_PARSER``
  config knob from *condor_dagman* and :tool:`condor_submit_dag`.
  :jira:`3971`

- Fixed a bug where HTCondor would use IPv4 to initiate a network
  connection despite configuration parameter :macro:`ENABLE_IPV4`
  being set to ``False``, and likewise for IPv6.
  :jira:`3970`

*** 26.0.2 bugs

*** 26.1.0 features

- Added :tool:`htcondor cluster`, which caches a cluster's job data
  locally and profiles it to produce a health report, flagging problems
  such as inefficient resource usage or held jobs and recommending
  specific follow-up commands to investigate them.
  :jira:`3892`

- :tool:`condor_gpu_discovery` now advertises an :ad-attr:`Integrated`
  attribute that is true for NVIDIA GPUs that share their memory with the
  host, such as unified-memory devices like the NVIDIA DGX Spark.
  :jira:`3899`

- The DAGMan Node Status File now reports aggregate job proc counts
  (submitted, running, idle, held, completed, and failed) for the DAG
  and each node, and can be written in JSON format.
  :jira:`3928`

- :tool:`condor_history` will now directly locate and read job records
  for a specified :ad-attr:`Owner` or :ad-attr:`ClusterId` when the
  Archive Librarian is in use.
  :jira:`3927`

- The Archive Librarian now removes users from its database once they have
  had no indexed jobs for :macro:`LIBRARIAN_USER_RETENTION_DAYS` days, which
  defaults to 365.
  :jira:`3943`

- The Archive Librarian now writes an address file,
  :macro:`LIBRARIAN_ADDRESS_FILE`, so it can be targeted by tools such as
  :tool:`condor_restart` with ``-daemon librarian``.
  :jira:`3943`

- The *condor_starter* can now optionally set a limit on the amount of
  compressed swap (zswap) a job may use, via the new
  :macro:`CGROUP_ZSWAP_MAX_EXPR`. It is a ClassAd expression, evaluated in
  the context of the slot and job ads, whose value in megabytes is written
  to the job's cgroup ``memory.zswap.max``. When it is unset, which is the
  default, HTCondor does not write to that control file at all, and the job
  gets whatever the system default is. Requires cgroup v2 and a kernel with
  zswap support.
  :jira:`3898`

- :tool:`condor_adstash` now includes a ``ndjsonfile`` interface which appends
  JSON per-line to adstash.jsonl in the directory specified by ``--json_dir``.
  :jira:`3959`

- Fixed a bug where the Archive Librarian's garbage collection removed only
  one archive file's records per pass and stopped just under
  :macro:`LIBRARIAN_HIGH_WATER_MARK`, instead of reducing the database to
  :macro:`LIBRARIAN_LOW_WATER_MARK`. Garbage collection also no longer
  mistakes a successful pass for a failed one, which triggered a
  :macro:`LIBRARIAN_GC_BACKOFF_SECONDS` delay, because the database file
  had not yet been checkpointed. The database file on disk now shrinks
  as soon as garbage collection finishes.
  :jira:`3943`

*** 26.1.0 bugs

- To assist in debugging, added :subcom:`min_condor_version` and
  :subcom:`max_condor_version`, which prevent the require the HTCondor
  version of the EP to greater than or equal to, or strictly less than,
  respectively, the specified version, e.g. "26.0.1".
  :jira:`3065`
*** 26.0.1 features

- HTCondor tarballs now contain `Pelican 26.0.0 <https://pelicanplatform.org/releases>`_

- The condor package now requires pelican-26.0.0.

*** 26.0.1 bugs

- Fixed a rare bug that could cause *condor_dagman* to crash when the
  AP is restarted.
  :jira:`3915`

